# Umami analytics, served first-party.
#
# These two rules must stay ABOVE the SPA catch-all: Netlify matches _redirects
# top to bottom and the first match wins, so /* would otherwise swallow them and
# hand back index.html.
#
# They exist so the tracker loads from consolelogic.net instead of umami.is,
# which EasyPrivacy blocks by hostname (||umami.is^$third-party). Unproxied,
# that silently drops every visitor running a content blocker, which is a large
# share of a developer audience.
#
# The two destinations are different hosts on purpose: the script is published
# from cloud.umami.is, but the tracker posts to gateway.umami.is. The /api/send
# path is fixed by the tracker (it appends it to data-host-url), so that rule
# cannot be renamed the way /js/stats.js can.
/js/stats.js  https://cloud.umami.is/script.js    200
/api/send     https://gateway.umami.is/api/send   200

# SPA fallback. Prerendered routes are real files in dist, and Netlify serves an
# existing file ahead of an unforced rewrite, so this only catches unknown paths.
/*  /index.html  200
